cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, the released models, or the committed
  out-of-fold predictions, please cite the paper (preferred-citation
  below). If you use the CirCor DigiScope dataset through this code,
  you must also cite CirCor - see THIRD_PARTY.md section 6.
title: >-
  mirasol2026: a low-cost AI stethoscope for resource-constrained
  heart murmur screening
abstract: >-
  Training, quantization, on-device benchmarking and analysis code for a
  fully offline heart-murmur screening prototype built on an Orange Pi
  Zero 2 W. Six CNN and transformer architectures are trained under one
  protocol on the CirCor DigiScope phonocardiogram dataset with
  patient-level five-fold cross-validation, exported to ONNX, and
  benchmarked on the target hardware. The repository regenerates every
  table and figure in the paper and its supplement.
type: software
authors:
